127
00:09:20,494 --> 00:09:23,140
But one thing to point out here, Claude didn't hit send.

128
00:09:23,374 --> 00:09:24,464
It's waiting for me to do that.

129
00:09:24,624 --> 00:09:29,104
Claw did all the work, but I'm still the person in the middle, which I think is still really important.

130
00:09:29,390 --> 00:09:37,664
Now the cool thing here is after I hit send and then my mom responds, it's going to take her ideas and it's going to put it in my Christmas tracker that I had to build.

131
00:09:37,902 --> 00:09:41,344
So if we go back to the dashboard, we can see that all eight tasks were completed.

132
00:09:41,504 --> 00:09:45,344
It estimated that it saved me about 9.5 hours for the day.

133
00:09:45,424 --> 00:09:49,732
And then my delegation score was 100, meaning that it was able to complete all the tasks.

134
00:09:50,064 --> 00:09:53,104
If we take a look in the folder here, you can see things that we asked for.

135
00:09:53,264 --> 00:09:57,104
For example, there's that 3D printer guide, and it actually made it look like a magazine.

136
00:09:57,230 --> 00:09:58,544
There's a flyer for my book.

137
00:09:58,624 --> 00:10:00,868
There's a study guide for my son's driver test.

138
00:10:01,102 --> 00:10:05,184
But take a look at this one, the 2027 planner that I asked for from my phone.

139
00:10:05,358 --> 00:10:08,784
This one looks really good, has all of the US holidays in it.

140
00:10:08,944 --> 00:10:14,224
There's a page for your big goals at the beginning of the year that, of course, has your calendar from January to December.

141
